* Next implementation work
** Manual admin commands
*** Add =/round close= to close the current open round immediately using
    the scheduled closure workflow.
*** Add =/round set-event-date= to move a finalized session to another date.
    Use it in the private server to move a session to tomorrow in the guild's
    timezone and exercise the reminder without waiting for the original date.
** Day-before session reminder
*** Use the local scheduler to send one reminder per upcoming finalized
    session when the guild reaches the day before its event date.
*** Find upcoming sessions even when a newer round is open. Cover sessions
    with and without an activity poll.
*** Move a finalized test session to tomorrow and confirm its reminder uses
    the updated date. Check that later scheduler runs send no duplicate.
** Hosting and round result
*** Add location or joining details to the round announcement.
*** If nobody eligible volunteers, switch to virtual when the round allows
    it and cancel when the round is in person only. Verify both outcomes in
    the private Discord server.
** Activity results follow-up
*** Validate the current publication triggers in the private Discord server.
*** If the cutoff arrives before all ballots are in, post partial totals. Post
    updated totals once everyone has voted, through the end of the event date
    in the guild's timezone. If everyone votes before the cutoff, post once.

* Recurring round creation
** Save the scheduling channel in guild settings and scope round actions to
   the intended channel and round state.
** Launch rounds automatically from the configured first survey date, launch
   time, timezone, and weekly or biweekly cadence.

* Manual Discord validation
** Use multiple legitimate, manually operated accounts in the private server.
** As a regular member, run =/preferences venue= to see the in-person default,
   then save Virtual and confirm it reads back privately. Open a round and
   check =host= and =virtualPreferenceUserIds= in MongoDB. Change that member's
   preference to In person and set another member's to Virtual. Open a second
   round and confirm that each round kept the preferences from when it opened.
   Confirm preferences survive =/round wipe=.
** For a round that offers either format, check the venue preselection,
   change it in the form, then reopen the form to confirm the change saved.
   Check that a virtual preference only changes the result when the member
   is available for the winning slot. After a virtual result, confirm that
   the next opening post only opens the in-person form.
** Check that the flexible venue picker can save an in-person hosting offer
   and that in-person-only rounds ask about hosting directly. Reopen each to
   check the previous answer. Switch a volunteer to virtual and verify that
   their hosting offer is withdrawn.
** Check that an eligible first-time host takes priority, then that the least
   recent host wins when all eligible volunteers have hosted. Verify that a
   volunteer who missed the winning slot is excluded.
** Check that members without Manage Server cannot use either wipe command.
   Check whether Discord hides the commands for those members.
** Check that creating a newer round cancels the previous open one and that
   a round with insufficient availability is cancelled at its deadline.
** Check that activity totals use the latest ballot when someone votes again
   and that =/round status= still lists the voter once.
** Check activity results for both early completion and the day-before cutoff
   with ballots still missing. Retest with a late final ballot after adding
   the second post.
** Check that a round with no eligible suggestions produces no activity poll.
** Run the full flow in the private server before deploying and rolling out
   to the real server.

* Maintenance
** Replace deprecated ephemeral reply options with Discord's flags API.
** Review free text input limits and sanitization. Keep secrets out of shared
   logs and interaction captures.
** Move validation out of workflow functions where that makes the core logic
   easier to read.
** clarify in suggestion input that they can browse activity history oustide of the modal/form
** don't say "your activity was unchanged", just say what their current suggestion is.

